      "summary": "The log processor can export sensitive free text when a message also contains a structured property. The other reviewed behavior appears to address the stated acceptance criteria.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 122,
          "message": "A message containing free text can bypass redaction when it also has a structured property, allowing credentials or other sensitive text into exported telemetry.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingLogProcessor treats any structured property as sufficient to keep the message, then RenderMessage substitutes placeholders in data.Body without redacting free text already present there. data.Body itself is also left unchanged.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs `logger.LogError(\"Authorization: \" + token + \" Case {Case}\", \"case-42\")`. The Case property makes hasLogProperties true, while the token is part of the message template rather than a redacted property. RenderMessage leaves it intact, so the formatted message and body can reach the exporter with the token. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
